type: software
title: "NOWA: Neural Networks with Reward-Based Learning and Evolutionary Architecture Growth"
abstract: >-
  NOWA is a cognitive architecture for a long-lived agent. Waking and sleep
  are separate: experience is recorded while awake, and slow memory is
  consolidated in sleep. Learning is local reward-prediction error, scaled by
  neuromodulators, with no backpropagation and no global loss. An
  eight-dimensional affect vector biases action. Inheritable module
  coefficients live in a genome, and a bounded set of consolidated traces may
  pass to offspring as an epigenome.
